},{"type":"Cross-link","start":61,"end":61,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2); alternate"},{"type":"Motif","start":79,"end":82,"description":"Nuclear localization signal"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":214,"end":214,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":301,"end":340,"description":"Important for interaction with IK"},{"type":"Region","start":380,"end":532,"description":"Necessary for interaction with NEK2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":428,"end":428,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":439,"end":480,"description":"Important for interaction with IK"},{"type":"Region","start":540,"end":551,"description":"Necessary for interaction with MAD2L1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":598,"end":598,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":610,"end":610,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":634,"end":634,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":716,"end":716,"description":"Phosphothreonine"}],"interfaces":{"MAD2L1":[529,530,533,534,535,537,538,539,540,541,542,543,544,545,546,547,548,549,550,553,554,556,557]},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Homodimer (PubMed:29162720, PubMed:9546394). Dimerizes via its N- and C- terminal regions (PubMed:29162720). Heterodimerizes with MAD2L1 in order to form a tetrameric MAD1L1-MAD2L1 core complex (PubMed:12006501, PubMed:18981471, PubMed:22351768, PubMed:9546394). Interacts with the closed conformation form of MAD2L1 (C-MAD2) and open conformation form of MAD2L1 (O-MAD2) (PubMed:29162720). It is unclear whether MAD1L1 dimerization promotes the conversion of closed to open conformation of MAD2L1 (PubMed:29162720). Formation of a heterotetrameric core complex containing two molecules each of MAD1L1 and of MAD2L1 promotes binding of another molecule of MAD2L1 to each MAD2L1, resulting in a heterohexamer (PubMed:12006501). Perturbation of the original MAD1L1-MAD2L1 structure by the spindle checkpoint may decrease MAD2L1 affinity for MAD1L1 (PubMed:12006501). CDC20 can compete with MAD1L1 for MAD2L1 binding, until the attachment and/or tension dampen the checkpoint signal, preventing further release of MAD2L1 on to CDC20 (PubMed:12006501). Also able to interact with the BUB1/BUB3 complex (PubMed:10198256). Interacts with NEK2 (PubMed:14978040). Interacts with TTK (PubMed:29162720). Interacts with TPR; the interactions occurs in a microtubule-independent manner (PubMed:18981471, PubMed:19273613, PubMed:20133940). Interacts with IK (PubMed:22351768). Interacts with the viral Tax protein (PubMed:9546394). Interacts with PRAP1 (PubMed:24374861)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q9Y6D9-3","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":626,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000402746.5"],"refseq":["NM_001304524.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001291453.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,1],[66,158,561]],"edits":[{"start":1,"end":157,"original":"MEDLGENTMVLSTLRSLNNFISQRVEGGSGLDISTSAPGS","replacement":"MLPARGCVRKRTVWPRLARVLIVTLLTLELSYAPLPCQLS","added":65}],"missing":156,"replaced":0,"novel":64,"foldedAbsent":113,"foldedMissing":113,"features":[[1,1,0],[2,112,0],[3,1,0],[4,1,0],[5,4,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q9Y6D9-3-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q9Y6D9-3-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":80.8,"plddt":[[0,42],[50,1],[0,5],[50,1],[0,14],[50,11],[70,2],[50,1],[70,18],[90,1],[70,2],[90,1],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,123],[70,14],[90,1],[70,1],[90,58],[70,1],[90,3],[70,21],[50,6],[0,4],[50,5],[70,48],[50,4],[0,8],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[70,8],[90,19],[70,8],[50,2],[70,9],[90,1],[70,1],[90,18],[70,1],[90,5],[70,2],[90,1],[70,11],[50,7],[0,9],[50,3],[70,6],[90,1],[70,1],[90,3],[70,1],[90,33],[70,3],[90,9],[70,4],[90,7],[70,7],[90,6],[70,1],[90,2],[70,1],[90,10],[70,1],[90,18],[70,4],[50,1]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"Q9Y6D9-4","name":"3","synonyms":["MAD1-beta"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","